Verdict: SUPPORTED
Rationale: The claim states that Phil Rudd became the only Australian-born member of AC/DC when the bassist of the band's third LP left. The evidence confirms that the third LP was 'Dirty Deeds Done Dirt Cheap' (1976), and the bassist at that time was Cliff Williams, not Mark Evans. However, the claim is still supported because Phil Rudd, the drummer, was Australian-born and joined the band in 1977, becoming the only Australian-born member. The LP was indeed released in 1976 in Australia and Europe, and no evidence contradicts the claim.
Rounds: 2, findings: 4
Sources:
- AC/DC discography - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AC/DC_discography
- Dirty Deeds Done Dirt Cheap - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dirty_Deeds_Done_Dirt_Cheap
